# Public (non-secret) config, committed to git on purpose so `next build` bakes it into the client bundle even
# when no real environment variables are present - e.g. the desktop app's GitHub Actions release build, which
# has no .env.local and (correctly) no repo secrets configured for these. None of this is sensitive: Firebase's
# own security model relies on Firestore/Storage rules, not on hiding this config, and the exact same values are
# already committed in apps/mobile/src/config/env.ts for the same reason. Real deployments are unaffected - Next
# always prefers actual environment variables (e.g. Vercel's dashboard-configured ones) over .env.production, so
# this file only ever fills a gap, never overrides anything.
#
# If you rotate the Firebase project, R2 bucket, or Cloudinary account, update this file AND
# apps/mobile/src/config/env.ts AND apps/desktop/src/web-app.js's getDesktopWebEnv() together.

